       pnmflip - replaced by pamflip


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppnnmmfflliipp was replaced in Netpbm 10.13 (December 2002) by ppaammfflliipp(1).

       ppaammfflliipp  is  mostly  backward compatible with ppnnmmfflliipp, but works on PAM
       images too.

       One way ppaammfflliipp is not backward compatible with ppnnmmfflliipp is that ppnnmmfflliipp
       lets  you specify any number of basic flip options, whereas ppaammfflliipp re‐
       quires exactly one.  (ppaammfflliipp provides the --xxffoorrmm option for requesting
       multiple  transformations,  though).   Because of this incompatibility,
       ppnnmmfflliipp still exists as a separate program, and all it does  is  trans‐
       late its options to ppaammfflliipp style and run ppaammfflliipp.

       You  should not make any new use of ppnnmmfflliipp and if you modify an exist‐
       ing use, you should upgrade to ppaammfflliipp.  But note that if you  write  a
       program that might have to be used with very old Netpbm, ppnnmmfflliipp is the
       only way to do that.

